WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.350
The last time she was here

2
00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:04.770
she told us how much she loved being a pen pal.

3
00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.260
And she's a good one and sends mail.

4
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:08.400
So please welcome back.

5
00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.120
The hilarious, beautiful and ever so stylish

6
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.833
Saturday night live cast member, Heidi Gardner.

7
00:00:14.833 --> 00:00:15.666
(audience applauding)

8
00:00:15.666 --> 00:00:16.499
Hi Drew

9
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.693
Okay. What time is that Heidi?

10
00:00:20.855 --> 00:00:21.688
Dear Drew

11
00:00:22.793 --> 00:00:24.142
(audience applauding)

12
00:00:24.142 --> 00:00:25.230
Okay, first thing we do

13
00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.000
is announce the zip code of the day.

14
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.380
And in honor of you it's...

15
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:34.053
64112 Kansas city, Missouri. My hometown.

16
00:00:34.053 --> 00:00:34.890
(audience applauding)

17
00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:38.270
I was so excited to celebrate Kansas city

18
00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:40.490
with you as we did it the news desk last time.

19
00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:42.890
And it's also the home of our affiliate station.

20
00:00:44.535 --> 00:00:46.050
KSHB TV channel 41.

21
00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:47.280
Hi guys.

22
00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.750
So Heidi, what are some fun facts about Kansas city?

23
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:54.450
Okay. Well, Kansas city has over 200 working fountains

24
00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:57.980
giving it the nickname of The City of Fountains.

25
00:00:57.980 --> 00:00:59.770
That's pretty cool.

26
00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:03.010
The Country Club Plaza opened in 1922.

27
00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:06.110
It's the US first suburban shopping district.

28
00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:09.540
And every thanksgiving the Plaza lights ceremony happens

29
00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.840
where a hometown hero flips the switch

30
00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.570
to turn on the Christmas lights.

31
00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:17.246
And I was so honored to have done it in 2019.

32
00:01:17.246 --> 00:01:19.156
(audience applauding)

33
00:01:19.156 --> 00:01:21.197
That must feel really good.

34
00:01:21.197 --> 00:01:23.630
Like, you know, it sometimes in life

35
00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:25.800
something tells you you're on the right track.

36
00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.630
Yes. It felt amazing.

37
00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:30.380
It was like just a sea of Kansas Citians

38
00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.780
out there supporting me to turn on lights.

39
00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.470
So it was really cool.

40
00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:36.340
Okay. Kansas city, Missouri

41
00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:37.830
would you please put pen to paper?

42
00:01:37.830 --> 00:01:39.590
We would love to hear from you.

43
00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:40.910
Please write us.

44
00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:42.260
I don't know how to describe it

45
00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:45.200
but there is something life affirming about mail.

46
00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:47.040
Yes. And it's how it used to be.

47
00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.630
Like, you get a letter in the mail you feel special.

48
00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:52.230
I mean, look at this envelope.

49
00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:56.034
If that doesn't bring you joy, then you're dead inside.

50
00:01:56.034 --> 00:01:56.867
(audience laughing)

51
00:01:56.867 --> 00:01:58.683
All right, let's open our first letter.

52
00:02:00.610 --> 00:02:03.303
Okay. I am going to open it right here.

53
00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.220
Dear drew,

54
00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:09.410
I lost two jobs at the start of the pandemic.

55
00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:12.030
So I've had to fall back on my art

56
00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:14.990
as my only means of income and therapy.

57
00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:16.210
Making my creations.

58
00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:19.290
I called them Rightmojis has really saved my life.

59
00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:22.490
The goal with my art is to bring a smile to people's faces.

60
00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:26.380
And I know you share the same sentiment with your show.

61
00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:27.213
Thank you.

62
00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.963
That is the goal, rightmoji.

63
00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:31.630
So as a thank you

64
00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.860
and hopefully to bring a smile to your face

65
00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:38.524
I created this Drew's news magnet as a gift for you.

66
00:02:38.524 --> 00:02:42.040
Okay. This is the cutest thing ever.

67
00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.170
This is so sweet

68
00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:45.330
and it does bring a huge smile to--

69
00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.420
Oh, there are multiples.

70
00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:48.863
Look at those.

71
00:02:48.863 --> 00:02:51.247
Oh, they're beautiful.

72
00:02:51.247 --> 00:02:53.860
(audience applauding)

73
00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:55.843
By the way, good blush.

74
00:02:56.710 --> 00:02:58.160
You look great.

75
00:02:58.160 --> 00:02:59.760
Well, rightmoji,

76
00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:01.640
I love these.

77
00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:04.420
And I'm going to send you $2,500

78
00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:07.850
that you can put towards just continuing your passion

79
00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:09.300
and doing what you do.

80
00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:11.270
And just to say thank you.

81
00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:12.820
And we recognize your work

82
00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:16.590
and admire it very much, Heidi, your turn.

83
00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:20.240
Drew I love what you were doing so much.

84
00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:24.356
So should we send another $2,500?

85
00:03:24.356 --> 00:03:27.058
(audience applauding)

86
00:03:27.058 --> 00:03:30.282
Yes...

87
00:03:30.282 --> 00:03:33.730
Please, please thank you Heidi.

88
00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:36.780
Thank you for letting me share the love.

89
00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:38.320
That's exactly right.

90
00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:40.520
All right Heidi, you have a letter

91
00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:43.270
sent from one of your pen pals, actually.

92
00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:44.490
I'd love for you to share.

93
00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:45.323
Okay.

94
00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:49.750
Dear Heidi,

95
00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:53.160
Thank you so much for thinking of us and sending a card.

96
00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:57.510
We have a therapy dog named Prada who visits every Saturday.

97
00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:59.360
We miss seing her and can't wait

98
00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.280
until she can come back to see us.

99
00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:04.650
We are also looking into therapy cats to visit.

100
00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:06.400
Your cat just had a birthday.

101
00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:09.270
Did your cat enjoy his tuna birthday cake?

102
00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:10.680
We hope he enjoyed it.

103
00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.550
From your friends at Seneca place.

104
00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.203
Verona, Pennsylvania.

105
00:04:16.468 --> 00:04:18.018
Oh, Heidi that's so sweet.

106
00:04:18.018 --> 00:04:20.400
No, I know.

107
00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.130
I love that.

108
00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:23.980
All right, we have time for one more.

109
00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:28.210
Hi Drew,

110
00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:29.601
I'm writing for some advice.

111
00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:31.530
Ooh...

112
00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:34.870 line:15%
I'm 20 years old and have never been on a first date.

113
00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:38.710 line:15%
It seems to me that you have been on well over 51st dates.

114
00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:39.760 line:15%
So I need your help.

115
00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:41.570
Give me everything you've got.

116
00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:44.010
Sincerely Angie.

117
00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.340
All right.

118
00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:46.570
Here's what I'm going to say.

119
00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:50.880
And it actually is directly related to 51st dates.

120
00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:54.830
The thing I fell in love with that story was to me

121
00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:56.760
it was a great allegory

122
00:04:56.760 --> 00:05:01.210
about someone who finds the energy to be kind

123
00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:03.090
to someone every day.

124
00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:07.070
And I think that that is the epitome of a good relationship.

125
00:05:07.070 --> 00:05:11.140
If you can find it in your heart to muster up kindness

126
00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:12.970
and patience and a sense of humor

127
00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:17.200
and maybe even a sense of adventure on a regular basis

128
00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:19.040
that's what 51st dates is about.

129
00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:21.290
And when you go on your first date

130
00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:22.800
maybe have that as an intention

131
00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.300
of someone you're looking for

132
00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:27.210
is going to be good to you on a daily basis.

133
00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:28.260
I love that.

134
00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:29.689
Really?

135
00:05:29.689 --> 00:05:30.522
(laughing)

136
00:05:30.522 --> 00:05:33.980
She's beautiful advice for anyone for a married woman.

137
00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:35.800
It's beautiful.

138
00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:39.220
All right, Heidi, do you have any advice for Angie?

139
00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:42.460
You know what? I do have some advice for Angie.

140
00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:44.220
You're 20 years old Angie,

141
00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:47.440
I bet you're a wonderful young woman

142
00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:51.630
and I just want to encourage you to be that young woman

143
00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:52.610
on your date.

144
00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:56.823 line:15%
Just have fun and be you and it's going to be great.

145
00:05:58.170 --> 00:05:59.003 line:15%
Yeah.

146
00:05:59.003 --> 00:05:59.836
I love that advice.

147
00:05:59.836 --> 00:06:00.870
It's so true.

148
00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:03.200
Well, if you need any help or advice

149
00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:06.290
or maybe want to see something or try something new,

150
00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:09.640
Then mail questions request photos and heartfelt

151
00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:13.860 line:15%
or funny stories to find out more and get our address.

152
00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:14.693 line:15%
Go to

153
00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:19.853
Well, should we say it together?

154
00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:24.103
Truly yours Drew and Heidi.

155
00:06:27.179 --> 00:06:29.762
(upbeat music)

